  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Polygenic inheritance and pleiotropy"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Polygenic traits are controlled by three or more genes, each adding a small effect, and they are also influenced by the environment. Human skin colour, for example, is thought to be controlled by three genes; AABBCC is darkest, aabbcc lightest, and intermediate genotypes give a range of shades. In pleiotropy a single gene affects several phenotypic traits: in phenylketonuria a single gene mutation causes mental retardation and reduced hair and skin pigmentation.",
    "kn": "ಬಹುಜೀನ್ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳನ್ನು ಮೂರು ಅಥವಾ ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಜೀನ್‌ಗಳು ನಿಯಂತ್ರಿಸುತ್ತವೆ, ಉದಾ: ಚರ್ಮದ ಬಣ್ಣ. ಬಹುಪರಿಣಾಮದಲ್ಲಿ ಒಂದು ಜೀನ್ ಅನೇಕ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ ಪರಿಣಾಮ ಬೀರುತ್ತದೆ, ಉದಾ: ಫಿನೈಲ್‌ಕೀಟೋನೂರಿಯಾ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Polygenic: many genes, additive effect, e.g. skin colour"
    },
    {
     "en": "Pleiotropy: one gene, many effects, e.g. phenylketonuria"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Polygenic traits are controlled by three or more genes, each adding a small effect, and they are also influenced by the environment. Human skin colour, for example, is thought to be controlled by three genes; AABBCC is darkest, aabbcc lightest, and intermediate genotypes give a range of shades. In pleiotropy a single gene affects several phenotypic traits: in phenylketonuria a single gene mutation causes mental retardation and reduced hair and skin pigmentation.",
    "kn": "ಬಹುಜೀನ್ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳನ್ನು ಮೂರು ಅಥವಾ ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಜೀನ್‌ಗಳು ನಿಯಂತ್ರಿಸುತ್ತವೆ, ಉದಾ: ಚರ್ಮದ ಬಣ್ಣ. ಬಹುಪರಿಣಾಮದಲ್ಲಿ ಒಂದು ಜೀನ್ ಅನೇಕ ಲಕ್ಷಣಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ ಪರಿಣಾಮ ಬೀರುತ್ತದೆ, ಉದಾ: ಫಿನೈಲ್‌ಕೀಟೋನೂರಿಯಾ."
   }
  },
