   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Sex determination"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Henking (1891) saw a nucleus he called the X body in some insect sperm. In grasshoppers, females are XX and males XO, so males have one chromosome fewer. In humans and Drosophila, males are XY and females XX: male heterogamety. In birds, females are ZW and males ZZ: female heterogamety. Honey bees follow haplodiploidy: an unfertilised egg develops into a haploid male (drone, 16 chromosomes) and a fertilised egg into a diploid female (queen or worker, 32 chromosomes).",
    "kn": "ಮಿಡತೆಯಲ್ಲಿ XO, ಮಾನವ ಮತ್ತು ಡ್ರೊಸೊಫಿಲಾದಲ್ಲಿ XY (ಪುರುಷ ಭಿನ್ನಗ್ಯಾಮೀಟಿ), ಹಕ್ಕಿಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ZW (ಸ್ತ್ರೀ ಭಿನ್ನಗ್ಯಾಮೀಟಿ). ಜೇನುಹುಳುಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಗಂಡು ಏಕಗುಣಿತ (16), ಹೆಣ್ಣು ದ್ವಿಗುಣಿತ (32)."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "XO: grasshopper; XY: humans, Drosophila"
    },
    {
     "en": "ZW (female heterogametic): birds"
    },
    {
     "en": "Honey bee: male n = 16, female 2n = 32"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Henking (1891) saw a nucleus he called the X body in some insect sperm. In grasshoppers, females are XX and males XO, so males have one chromosome fewer. In humans and Drosophila, males are XY and females XX: male heterogamety. In birds, females are ZW and males ZZ: female heterogamety. Honey bees follow haplodiploidy: an unfertilised egg develops into a haploid male (drone, 16 chromosomes) and a fertilised egg into a diploid female (queen or worker, 32 chromosomes).",
    "kn": "ಮಿಡತೆಯಲ್ಲಿ XO, ಮಾನವ ಮತ್ತು ಡ್ರೊಸೊಫಿಲಾದಲ್ಲಿ XY (ಪುರುಷ ಭಿನ್ನಗ್ಯಾಮೀಟಿ), ಹಕ್ಕಿಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ZW (ಸ್ತ್ರೀ ಭಿನ್ನಗ್ಯಾಮೀಟಿ). ಜೇನುಹುಳುಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಗಂಡು ಏಕಗುಣಿತ (16), ಹೆಣ್ಣು ದ್ವಿಗುಣಿತ (32)."
